# How to add a simple component

Pattern: one folder per component, single root element, styles from tokens. The existing `Header`, `Footer` and `Menu` follow it.

## Step-by-step

1. Create `src/components/<Name>/`:

   ```
   src/components/<Name>/
   ├── index.tsx
   └── <Name>.module.scss
   ```

   Add a `constants.ts` only for static data the component maps over (see `Menu/constants.tsx`).

2. Define props as an interface in `index.tsx`. Accept `className` on the root when the component is reused in more than one place:

   ```tsx
   interface ButtonProps {
     variant?: 'primary' | 'secondary'
     isLoading?: boolean
     className?: string
     children: ReactNode
   }
   ```

3. Write styles in `<Name>.module.scss`. **Never** hardcode hex or raw breakpoints — use the tokens in `src/styles/settings.scss` and the mixins (rule 12). Load mixins only when the module uses them:

   ```scss
   @use 'mixins' as *;

   .button {
     padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
     color: var(--color-bg);
     background-color: var(--color-primary);
     border-radius: 4px;

     @media (hover: hover) {
       &:hover {
         opacity: 0.9;
       }
     }

     &:focus-visible {
       outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
       outline-offset: 2px;
     }

     &[disabled] {
       cursor: not-allowed;
       opacity: 0.5;
     }

     @include b-up(md) {
       padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
     }
   }
   ```

   Child elements use BEM-style nesting: `.header { &__logo { … } }` compiles to `.header__logo`, consumed as `s.header__logo`. Modifiers use `--`: `s['menu--footer']`.

4. Implement `index.tsx` as an **arrow-function component** with a default export (ESLint enforces arrow functions). Compose classes with `cn` (rule 14). No `import React` — import types by name:

   ```tsx
   import type { ReactNode } from 'react'
   import cn from 'classnames'

   import s from './Button.module.scss'

   const Button = ({
     variant = 'primary',
     isLoading = false,
     className,
     children,
   }: ButtonProps) => (
     <button
       type="button"
       className={cn(s.button, s[`button--${variant}`], className)}
       disabled={isLoading}
       aria-busy={isLoading || undefined}
     >
       {children}
     </button>
   )

   export default Button
   ```

5. Add `'use client'` only when the component needs hooks, browser APIs or event handlers (as `Menu` does). Everything else stays a server component.

6. Import it through the alias: `import Button from '~components/Button'`.

7. Run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npx stylelint "src/**/*.scss"`; all must pass with zero warnings before handing off.
